---
// LAUF-2026-09-10.md Teil C / C3 point 1: fields rebuilt to match
// docs/mockups/kontakt-prototype.dc.html (Version A) — Name, E-Mail,
// Anliegen, Nachricht. The phone field this used to have isn't in the
// prototype and isn't asked for anywhere else on record, so it's dropped
// rather than kept as an unexplained extra. Still not wired to a real
// backend — see TODO below; honeypot and the consent checkbox stay
// regardless of the mockup not showing them, since they're independent
// legal/anti-spam needs, not a visual design choice.
---

<!--
  Backend, 2026-09-13 (docs/decisions.md): Microsoft Forms turned out not
  to work as a plain <form> target (it only accepts submissions through
  its own hosted page, not an external POST), and web3forms was dropped
  for processing the message on US servers — see that entry for both.
  Posts instead to public/kontakt-senden.php, a small script that runs on
  easyname (the site's own host) and forwards straight to Marina's inbox;
  nothing is stored anywhere in between.
-->
<!--
  Live-Korrektur, 2026-09-13: `novalidate` kam offenbar unbesehen aus dem
  Claude-Design-Prototypen mit (der eine eigene JS-Validierung hatte, die
  hier nie mitgebaut wurde, siehe LAUF-2026-09-10.md C3) und blieb ohne
  Ersatz stehen — Pflichtfelder (Name, E-Mail, Anliegen, Zustimmung)
  hatten dadurch faktisch keine Prüfung: ein leeres Formular ließ sich
  klicklos absenden, ohne jede Rückmeldung. Entfernt, damit die native
  HTML5-Validierung (required/type="email") greift — funktioniert ganz
  ohne JavaScript, keine eigene Validierungslogik nötig. Kein Ersatz für
  das fehlende echte Absendeziel (weiterhin offen), aber verhindert
  zumindest, dass unvollständige Anfragen unbemerkt "durchgehen". -->
<form class="contact-form" method="post" action="/kontakt-senden.php">
  <div class="field">
    <label for="contact-name">Dein Name *</label>
    <input id="contact-name" name="name" type="text" required autocomplete="name" />
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <label for="contact-email">E-Mail *</label>
    <input id="contact-email" name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email" />
  </div>

  {/* C3 point 2: the prototype offers three options ("Frage zu
     Persephone" / "Kooperation & Presse" / "Sonstiges"); the brief
     elsewhere calls for four and explicitly no fifth — a real
     contradiction between the two records. These three are kept because
     the prototype is the newer decision, per C3's own instruction; see
     the handoff report for the discrepancy. */}
  <div class="field field-wide">
    <label for="contact-topic">Anliegen *</label>
    <select id="contact-topic" name="topic" required>
      <option value="">Bitte wählen…</option>
      <option value="frage">Frage zu Persephone</option>
      <option value="kooperation">Kooperation & Presse</option>
      <option value="sonstiges">Sonstiges</option>
    </select>
  </div>

  <div class="field field-wide">
    <label for="contact-message">Deine Nachricht</label>
    <textarea id="contact-message" name="message" rows="5"></textarea>
  </div>

  {/* Honeypot — hidden from sighted/keyboard users; a filled-in value
      means a bot submitted the form. */}
  <div class="field honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
    <label for="contact-website">Website</label>
    <input id="contact-website" name="website" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
  </div>

  <div class="field field-wide consent">
    <label>
      <input type="checkbox" name="consent" required />
      Ich stimme zu, dass meine Daten zur Bearbeitung meiner Anfrage verarbeitet werden. Mehr dazu
      in der <a href="/datenschutz/">Datenschutzerklärung</a>.
    </label>
  </div>

  {/* NACHTLAUF-2026-09-08.md B7: live says "Senden", not "Nachricht senden". */}
  <button type="submit" class="button button-primary field-wide submit-button">Senden</button>
</form>

<style>
  .contact-form {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .field label {
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .field input,
  .field select,
  .field textarea {
    padding: 0.7rem 1rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid rgba(24, 26, 43, 0.25);
    font: inherit;
    min-height: 44px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .field textarea {
    min-height: 120px;
    resize: vertical;
  }

  .honeypot {
    position: absolute;
    left: -9999px;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .consent {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .consent label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .consent input {
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
    min-height: auto;
  }

  /* Grid's own default (justify-items: stretch) was filling the button's
     whole grid cell — full form width — since .button's own inline-flex
     sizing only controls its content, not the outer grid-item box.
     "button wrap um text" (screenshot feedback): hug its own label. */
  .submit-button {
    justify-self: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .contact-form {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }

    .field-wide {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
</style>
